<VULN>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Num</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>V-253272</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Severity</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>low</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Group_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_ID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SV-253272r1268251_rule</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Ver</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>WN11-00-000085</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Standard local user accounts must not exist on a system in a domain.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Discuss</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>To minimize potential points of attack, local user accounts, other than built-in accounts and local administrator accounts, must not exist on a workstation in a domain. Users must log on to workstations in a domain with their domain accounts.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>IA_Controls</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Run "Computer Management".

Navigate to System Tools &gt;&gt; Local Users and Groups &gt;&gt; Users.

If local users other than the accounts listed below exist on a workstation in a domain, this is a finding. 

The accounts listed assumes a system is joined to a domain and thus (per best practice), the local default accounts have been disabled.

For standalone or nondomain-joined systems, this is Not Applicable.

Built-in guest account (SID ending in 501)
Built-in DefaultAccount (SID ending in 503)
Built-in defaultuser0 (*SID unique per workstation)
Built-in WDAGUtilityAccount (SID ending in 504)
Local administrator account(s)

* Note: The SID for defaultuser0 is machine-specific and immutable (cannot be changed). It will differ per Windows installation.

Some of the built-in accounts may not exist on a system, depending on the Windows 11 version.
Refer to WN11-SO-000280 for requirement/guidance in use of Windows LAPS to manage the built-in administrator account password.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Limit local user accounts on domain-joined systems. Remove any unauthorized local accounts.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
